WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.365
The animal crossed the street because it was tired.

00:00:03.365 --> 00:00:05.234
What does it refer to?

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:07.104
You probably chose the animal.

00:00:07.104 --> 00:00:08.973
But change tired to wide,

00:00:08.973 --> 00:00:11.590
and the street becomes a better answer.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.834
The word it stayed the same.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.825
Its meaning changed with the words around it.

00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:20.563
This is the problem at the heart of the Transformer:

00:00:20.563 --> 00:00:24.302
how can a machine build a representation of a word

00:00:24.302 --> 00:00:25.798
that reflects its context?

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:29.476
Imagine reading the sentence from the position of it.

00:00:29.476 --> 00:00:33.523
The model makes a query for that position and a

00:00:33.523 --> 00:00:36.356
key for every position in the sentence.

00:00:36.356 --> 00:00:39.999
Comparing the query with each key gives a score.

00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:42.832
A bigger score means a stronger connection.

00:00:42.832 --> 00:00:44.856
The model then blends information,

00:00:44.856 --> 00:00:47.689
called values, using those connections as weights.

00:00:47.689 --> 00:00:50.522
The highlighted line illustrates one possible connection.

00:00:50.522 --> 00:00:52.141
It is an example,

00:00:52.141 --> 00:00:54.569
not a measurement from the paper.

00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:58.926
One set of connections gives you one view of the

00:00:58.926 --> 00:01:02.401
sentence. A Transformer builds several views at once.

00:01:02.401 --> 00:01:05.441
Each attention head has different learned settings,

00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:08.481
so different heads can emphasize different relationships.

00:01:08.481 --> 00:01:12.824
The model combines their outputs into a new representation for

00:01:12.824 --> 00:01:16.298
each word. It also adds information about position.

00:01:16.298 --> 00:01:20.641
Otherwise, attention would have no way to tell whether animal

00:01:20.641 --> 00:01:23.247
came before street or after it.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.081
Why did this matter for translation?

00:01:26.081 --> 00:01:30.799
A recurrent encoder passes information from one position to the

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:35.518
next. Attention lets distant words interact within a single layer,

00:01:35.518 --> 00:01:39.292
and an encoder can update all positions together.

00:01:39.292 --> 00:01:41.652
In the paper's English-to-German experiment,

00:01:41.652 --> 00:01:44.011
the Transformer reached 28.4 BLEU,

00:01:44.011 --> 00:01:45.898
a translation quality score.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:50.616
There are trade-offs. Standard attention compares every pair of positions,

00:01:50.616 --> 00:01:55.335
and the decoder still generates the translation one word at

00:01:55.335 --> 00:02:00.053
a time. The advance was changing how context is computed.
